The doctor examines me with a stethoscope.
He tells me to take a deep breath.
I have a slight pain in my chest.
"You have a bad cold," he says.
"That is why your throat hurts."
He writes a prescription for me.
He gives me some instructions.
"You must always drink hot water."
"Do not drink cold water," he says.
"You must take this medicine after meals."
"The rain is heavy these days."
"So you should not go outside."
"You must rest well at home."
I listen to everything carefully.
"If you take this, you will get well soon," he says.
"If you are still not feeling well after two days, you must come again."
I thank the doctor.
I take the prescription and walk out of the room.
